Description: EGL Pi5 — HEVC multi-plane EGL import diagnostics (debug-only)
 Patch 0013 (the per-plane modifier hypothesis) was invalidated by runtime
 logs: every HEVC NV12 import goes through the !plane_index_.has_value()
 multi-plane branch, never the per-plane branch the old patch fixed. The
 multi-plane branch already pushes per-plane modifiers correctly, yet the
 green frame persists with no eglCreateImageKHR error.
 .
 This iteration drops the dead per-plane fix and instead instruments the
 multi-plane import + the eglCreateImageKHR result, so we can see whether:
   * dma-buf offset/pitch values match SAND128 tiled layout expectations,
   * MakeScopedEGLImage actually succeeds (no silent EGL error),
   * the attrs list is the size we expect for n_planes=2 with modifiers.
 .
 All additions are LOG(ERROR) markers under the AGORA_DEBUG_0013 prefix.
 No functional change to chromium's image-import logic.
Author: Steve Slivinski <sslivins@github.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-22
